                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8845664c-aba8-3ea7-91ad-eca62c503ec9",
                        "entry_id": "db496b33-d8bf-3924-b622-43fb2b859f52",
                        "glosses": [
                            "утеплённый сапог для холодного и очень холодного климата"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "обычно мн.ч."
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "02c02bca-20ad-4354-9382-dd0562f38104",
                                "sense_id": "8845664c-aba8-3ea7-91ad-eca62c503ec9",
                                "text": "Но несмотря на то, что я полностью отключился от реальности, я автоматически продолжал давить на педали, сильно отводя в сторону правое колено — так меньше чувствовалась мозоль, которую мне успел натереть унт."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1360e345-8545-4cc5-a016-3383f7c7cf6a",
                                "sense_id": "8845664c-aba8-3ea7-91ad-eca62c503ec9",
                                "text": "Поскольку летел я на Полюс, то несмотря на теплый московский май, одет был соответственно — в унты, меховые брюки и выданный нам толстый водолазный свитер."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "568e6272-57f1-4684-846e-01874ae2250d",
                        "source_entry_id": "db496b33-d8bf-3924-b622-43fb2b859f52",
                        "source_sense_id": "8845664c-aba8-3ea7-91ad-eca62c503ec9",
                        "target_lang_word": "flying boot",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8ef02455-1cbc-46dd-96b3-b78ed93d539d",
                        "source_entry_id": "db496b33-d8bf-3924-b622-43fb2b859f52",
                        "source_sense_id": "8845664c-aba8-3ea7-91ad-eca62c503ec9",
                        "target_lang_word": "mukluk",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mukluk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75c26b27-861b-31ac-b3a9-2224bab69bd7",
                                        "entry_id": "38031374-afb3-3b30-8812-735a01572613",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A soft knee-high boot of sealskin or reindeer skin, originally worn by Inuit and Yupik."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Canada",
                                            "US"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ddf06ec-bc83-48bd-b67f-f66e1b93f4c5",
                                                "sense_id": "75c26b27-861b-31ac-b3a9-2224bab69bd7",
                                                "text": "Her parkee, made of Caribou, it is a lovely fit, / And she's all right from muck-a-luck unto her dainty mit. / This lovely Klooch is fond of Hooch, and makes it very well."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43aed2dd-4e52-3c57-b2cb-5985f5428aad",
                                        "entry_id": "38031374-afb3-3b30-8812-735a01572613",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A laced winter boot resembling a traditional mukluk, with thick rubber sole and cloth upper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Canada",
                                            "US"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf0bc87d-56d7-4446-a3fb-fcc69c40a495",
                                                "sense_id": "43aed2dd-4e52-3c57-b2cb-5985f5428aad",
                                                "text": "[...] the Canadians’ [soldiers’] mukluks and sleeping bags were superior to anything in use. the mukluk, a rubber-soled boot with a calf-high outer nylon cover, has a thick woollen inner boot that keeps feet warm in the coldest of weather."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5e8f389-6e48-4c74-ab23-d03e7752aa46",
                                                "sense_id": "43aed2dd-4e52-3c57-b2cb-5985f5428aad",
                                                "text": "The skin is used to make mukluks, hats, parkas. We are resourceful and respectful of the animals, the land."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
